{
  "_notes": "The Diocese of Austin (erected 1947), a suffragan see of Galveston-Houston: twenty-five counties from the Hill Country to the Brazos, Waco to San Marcos. The parishes are real churches by name and place; founding years and coordinates are as best known and FLAGGED FOR VERIFICATION against the diocesan directory (a year may be the mission's or the parish's; a coordinate is the church's block, not its door). The kinds, the people, the money, and everything else roll. The diocese has no major seminary of its own; its men are formed out of the diocese (St. Mary's in Houston, Assumption in San Antonio, Holy Trinity in Irving for college), and the preset names one of them. Nobody real is named. St. Francis of Assisi in Franklin (Robertson County) is kept as a rural parish by name; its founding year is a guess to verify. The campus block names the Newman posting for this diocese: St. Mary's at Texas A&M (systems: engine/study.ts, events/study/aggie.json).",
