  "voice": {
    "weather": [
      "January is cedar fever: half the pews coughing through the homily and the other half pretending not to.",
      "In April the bluebonnets come up along the highway to the mission churches and every parish bulletin has a photograph of them.",
      "The August that does not end: a hundred and five at the four o'clock wedding, and the air conditioning the parish council voted down in March.",
      "The first cold front comes through in October like a door slamming, and the whole diocese goes to Mass in a jacket it bought for it."
    ],
    "sunday": [
      "Sunday is three Masses in two languages and a mission church forty minutes out, and the pastor eats lunch in the truck.",
      "Sunday at the campus chaplaincy is nine hundred students at nine at night and a line for confession that runs down the stairs.",
      "Sunday in the Blackland is the painted church full of families whose great-grandfathers built it, and a priest from Nigeria who has learned the Czech hymns."
    ],
    "presbyterate": [
      "The presbyterate meets at the retreat house on the lake and argues about the Spanish Mass schedule, the mission churches, and whether the diocese needs its own seminary.",
      "Half the priests were formed in Houston or San Antonio and the other half overseas, and the deanery dinners are where they find out they agree.",
      "The men who came out of the campus chaplaincies are a generation now, pastors in their forties, and the chancery is theirs whether the older men like it or not."
    ]
  },
